              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ūsūra, ūsūrae — \"interest charged; use\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ūsūra gravis erat. The interest was heavy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ūsūra, ūsūrae f., built on ūtor, to use: payment for the use of money, often plural. English usury."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ūsūra is built on ūtor, ūsus \"to use\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): payment for the use of money. English usury comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
