          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pignus comes from the root of pangō \"to fasten, to fix\" (Lewis & Short), the root also in pacīscor \"to make a bargain\": a thing that fastens a bargain."
            }
          ]
        },
